  "query_preview": "..Dry and relatively stable westerly aloft, along with \nrising hghts, will define much of the upcoming forecast period. This \nmeans a warming trend, with temperatures rising to around normal and \nthen above normal for the next several days. Daytime winds will stay \nin the normal, diurnal range, nothing that will bring any impacts. \nAs far as moisture, as we stated, things are pretty dry. However, we \nexpect hghts to rise enough by Wednesday/Thursday that some moisture \nmay sneak in under the ridge from the east and southeast. This could \nlead to some convective activity, but even that possibility will be \nshort-lived, as dry westerlies move back into the forecast by next \nweekend.",
